# {{project_name}}

A streaming payments contract that releases a token continuously over time,
generated by [soroban-forge](https://github.com/soroban-forge-labs/soroban-forge)
from the `streaming` template.

## How it works

1. **Fund** — the sender deposits the full stream amount into the contract.
2. **Linear release** — tokens stream continuously at a constant rate from
   `initialize` until `duration_seconds` has elapsed.
3. **Claim** — the recipient calls `claim` to transfer any newly streamed
   tokens to their address, pro-rata to elapsed time. Can be called multiple
   times, including mid-stream.

## Develop

```sh
cargo test                 # run unit tests
stellar contract build     # build the deployable wasm
```

## Deploy to testnet

```sh
stellar contract deploy \
  --wasm target/wasm32v1-none/release/{{crate_name}}.wasm \
  --source-account <your-identity> \
  --network testnet
```

Then initialize and fund:

```sh
stellar contract invoke \
  --id <CONTRACT_ID> \
  --source-account <SENDER> \
  --network testnet \
  -- initialize \
  --sender <SENDER_ADDRESS> \
  --token <TOKEN_ADDRESS> \
  --recipient <RECIPIENT_ADDRESS> \
  --duration_seconds 2592000 \
  --total_amount 1000000

stellar contract invoke \
  --id <CONTRACT_ID> \
  --source-account <SENDER> \
  --network testnet \
  -- fund
```

The recipient claims streamed tokens:

```sh
stellar contract invoke \
  --id <CONTRACT_ID> \
  --source-account <RECIPIENT> \
  --network testnet \
  -- claim
```

